The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. For the input fence[ S A ], the last object inside a code fence is A, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of A. For the rewritten text fence[ S A ] B, the last object inside a code fence is still A, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of A. Since the fenced object remains A, the answer stays unchanged.